# Documentation toolchain — top-level pins (input to pip-compile).
#
# This file lists the DIRECT documentation-build dependencies for the MkDocs +
# Backstage TechDocs site. Exact, fully-resolved, hash-pinned versions are
# generated into requirements-docs.txt via:
#
#     pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-docs.txt requirements-docs.in
#
# The Documentation CI workflow (.github/workflows/docs.yml) installs the
# compiled, hashed requirements-docs.txt so every build resolves the identical
# dependency tree (supply-chain determinism — see review finding P7-2).
#
# techdocs-core >= 1.0.2 is required for correct Mermaid rendering; 1.7.0 is the
# version validated against this repository's docs set.
#
# SECURITY (residual risk — documentation only): techdocs-core==1.7.0 (the latest
# release) transitively hard-pins pymdown-extensions==10.21.3, which carries a
# Medium path-traversal advisory in its pymdownx.b64 extension (GHSA-9xwg-3r6f-jcx2
# / CVE-2026-61632, CVSS 5.3). The fix (pymdown-extensions>=11.0) cannot be adopted
# in isolation — recompiling this file with it yields ResolutionImpossible against
# the techdocs-core wheel's ==10.21.3 constraint — and the vulnerable extension is
# not enabled (mkdocs.yml configures only pymdownx.superfences), so the sink is
# unreachable. Do not bump until techdocs-core relaxes the pin. Full rationale:
# the pymdown-extensions security note in LIBRARIES.md (Rule F / AAP §0.9.2).

mkdocs-techdocs-core==1.7.0
mkdocs-mermaid2-plugin==1.2.3
